    "body": "## Bounded ragged decode segment selection; full acceptance passed, total gain unresolved\nRuntime e972997 passed full Level3 **102/105**, fixed warmed single-round4K **5766.410667** tok/s and16K **4048.277609** tok/s, complete requests/tokens and TTFT **3594.68/124268.06ms**. Compared with PR28's separate rounds, deltas are only+0.0104%/+0.0035%; do not claim these as an established model speedup. Remains Draft pending weighted complete-cost/increment decision.\n\nChanges are limited to default target256,2KV heads,builder16: B29/30 choose4 segments andB60..63 choose2; preserve PR28 B40=16 and every other case. Original producer/reducer and eligibility/wrapper ASTs stay unchanged. CPU28784 chooser cases and440 device component cases pass, including random packed KV, ragged lengths, NaN scratch, independent CPU FP64 and changed-input Graph. Selected component cases show consistent local positive timings; exact raw rounds remain archived.\n\n## New actual runtime coverage\nPR32 v5 diagnostic (production identical to e972997) now confirms the six selected eager grids really execute: **16800** GQA kernel launches at4K and **31206** at16K. One actual Llama model, zero audit errors. FULL captures/replays are excluded; these are not total attention counts or device-time measurements. Evidence: PR32 `docs/evidence/short-query-rope-audit-20261024/v5-final/`, shared at c89ad4a.\n\nCoverage no longer blocks evaluation, but it does not establish incremental service gain or weighted device cost. Keep the positive component evidence and full accepted scores; do not discard the whole attention direction or substitute diagnostic timing for acceptance. Exact runtime/source/SO hashes and raw accepted scores are in this PR's service-final evidence.\n"
